  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "If $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-8$ and $f(-8)=25,$ then what is \n${lim}_{x\\to (-8)^{-}}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{f(x)}}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-8,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-8)^{-}}f(x)=f(-8)=25.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-8)^{-}}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{f(x)}}=\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{25}}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
